\textbf{Label content is secondary.} Random OCC and Full OCC differ by 0.9 percentage points in CAR, a gap within cross-seed variance. Random binary labels---containing no spatial information---match structured occupancy labels in collision avoidance, consistent with gradient flow regularization as the primary factor rather than spatial content. This comparison is preliminary at 2 vs.\ 3 seeds.

\textbf{Full OCC advantage is checkpoint-sensitive.} At an earlier checkpoint (step 47{,}500), Full OCC and Vanilla yield identical mean CAR (0.780), suggesting that the 1.7pp advantage at step 50{,}000 emerges late in training and is sensitive to checkpoint selection. The gradient flow ordering (Random OCC $>$ Full OCC $>$ Vanilla $>$ Detach OCC) is consistent at both checkpoints, but the magnitude of the Full OCC--Vanilla gap depends on the evaluation point.

\textbf{TSR remains stable.}
